INDEPENDENT VERIFICATION OF #466 (perm gate) + #467 (borrow pairs) — compose-6
================================================================================

Host     Apple M4 Pro, 8P+4E (12 logical), Darwin 25.5.0.
Base     main 8568dbb. Both branches root there (merge-base == 8568dbb for both;
         checked FIRST, no stale branch point).
Compose  verify/compose-6 = main + origin/fix/perm-gate-aarch64 + origin/perf/borrow-pairs.
Build    cargo build --release --no-default-features --features "bitdepth_8,bitdepth_16".
         No -C target-cpu=native. Builds niced; NO nice on any timed run.
Data     verify_compose6_gap_2026-08-08.tsv (224 rows = 4 arms x 8 cells x 7 rounds)

BOX WAS NOT IDLE. Another agent's benchmark (~/tmp/sitecls/bin/bench_cls) ran
through most of the sweep; the strict idle gate starved (1 cell committed in
3 min), so the run used ALLOW_LOAD=1 and records the foreign count per row.
172 of 224 rows carry foreign>0. Arms interleave with rotating order inside
every cell, so PAIRED RATIOS hold; ABSOLUTE ms are inflated. The idle-only
subset (n=1..3) gives the same headline to three digits, which is the check
that the ratios survived: base/dav1d_fd1 at 8bpc t=1 is 1.368 loaded, 1.374
idle-only, and 1.368 in the pairs branch's own idle run.


1. GAP TO dav1d 1.5.4 — median of 7, two-point wall fit (2 and 20 frames)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                head/base   bands     base/ref  head/ref   ms short of 1.30x
  8bpc  t=1      0.9382   disjoint     1.368     1.283          -4.2   <- MET
  8bpc  t=2      0.9970   OVERLAP      1.584     1.579          35.5
  8bpc  t=4      1.0168   OVERLAP      1.731     1.760          30.7
  8bpc  t=8      0.9815   OVERLAP      1.945     1.909          23.5
  10bpc t=1      0.9421   disjoint     1.512     1.425          31.6
  10bpc t=2      1.0126   OVERLAP      1.597     1.617          41.0
  10bpc t=4      1.0549   OVERLAP      1.665     1.756          31.1
  10bpc t=8      1.0072   OVERLAP      1.957     1.971          26.6
  ref = dav1d_fd1 (--framedelay 1). dav1d_def is 0-4% faster at t>1.

  The ~1.30x bar is met at exactly ONE of eight cells (8bpc t=1, 1.283).
  Reproduces the pairs branch's own claim (1.368 -> 1.294 8bpc t=1,
  1.520 -> 1.437 10bpc t=1) on an independent run with a different load
  profile. t>1 is null in BOTH directions — every band overlaps.

  t1 -> t8 scaling:  base 4.54x / head 4.34x / dav1d_fd1 6.46x / dav1d_def 6.71x
                     (10bpc: 4.94 / 4.62 / 6.39 / 6.78)


2. PER-BUCKET PROFILE — /usr/bin/sample self-time leaves via
   scripts/perf/sample_selftime.py + scripts/perf/bucket_selftime.py,
   30 s per arm on v4k_8tile 8bpc; ms/frame = bucket share x the wall fit above.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  t=1        base %   base ms/f     head %   head ms/f
  entropy    64.96      221.1       68.37      218.4
  tracker    12.73       43.3        9.42       30.1
  kernels    18.37       62.5       18.16       58.0
  runtime     1.26        4.3        1.17        3.7
  other       2.68        9.1        2.87        9.2
  TOTAL                 340.4                  319.4

  Tracker 43.3 -> 30.1 ms/f is ~63% of the 21.0 ms/f wall win; the rest lands
  in kernels/entropy, where `sample` attributes inlined tracker code to the
  caller. The 43.3 ms/f base figure agrees with the 41.7 ms/f that #465's
  bucket profile reported — independent instrument, same number.

  t=8 head: entropy 38.93 / tracker 18.06 / kernels 13.53 / runtime 3.05 /
  other 26.43 (of which __psynch_cvwait 20.06 = worker idle). These are shares
  of CPU time across 8 threads, not of wall.


3. WHY t>1 CANNOT REACH 1.30x — confirmed from the pairs branch's own
   decomposition data (borrow_pairs_decomp_2026-08-08.tsv, recomputed here)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  8bpc t=8: base 65.2, ship 65.6, tinynop 63.8, untracked 45.9, dav1d 34.4.
  untracked/dav1d = 1.332. A tracker costing NOTHING still misses the bar at
  t=8. The residual is scaling (4.3-4.6x vs dav1d's 6.4-6.8x), not borrow cost.


