6. DEFECT FOUND — PR #467 breaks CI on the `asm` leg (NOT reported by its author)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  main 8568dbb  CI success.  #466 (f0547d0)  CI success, 21/21 jobs.
  #467 (5580533)  CI FAILURE: "Build & Test (ubuntu-latest, asm)".

  Cause: the branch's new `row_guard_policy_tests` assert tracker behaviour, and
  the `asm` config implies `unchecked`, which compiles borrow tracking out. Both
  tests then fail — including on purpose, via their own anti-vacuity assertion
  ("tracking is off in this build and this test gates nothing"). The design
  intent is right; the cfg gate is missing.

  Reproduced locally, exactly:
    cargo test --release --no-default-features \
      --features "bitdepth_8,bitdepth_16,unchecked" --lib
    base    69 passed; 0 failed
    compose 69 passed; 2 failed  <- only the two new tests; nothing else moves.

  Fix is one attribute, using the idiom already in tree (src/disjoint_mut.rs:29,
  src/safe_simd/pixel_access.rs:451, ...):
    -#[cfg(test)]
    +#[cfg(all(test, not(feature = "unchecked")))]
     mod row_guard_policy_tests {

  NOT a regression, checked and dismissed: the `disjoint-mut CI` failures on
  #467 ("Test --no-default-features" x3, "Test --all-features") are PRE-EXISTING
  on main — reproduced identically on both trees (23 and 2 errors respectively).
  That workflow is path-filtered on crates/rav1d-disjoint-mut/**, so it simply
  never fired on #466 or on recent main pushes.

  Also pre-existing, both trees identical: `cargo clippy --all-targets
  -D warnings` fails on aarch64 (dead code in src/safe_simd/itx_arm*.rs, plus
  examples/md5_inventory.rs, examples/md5_ablate.rs, examples/bench_ivf_limit.rs,
  benches/tier_isolation.rs). CI pins Clippy to x86_64 where those are cfg'd out.


